  "title": "Ghana gains independence",
  "summary": "On 6 March 1957 the Gold Coast, with Ashanti, the Northern Territories Protectorate and British Togoland, became independent from Britain as Ghana, with Kwame Nkrumah of the Convention People's Party as first prime minister. A ceremony was held at the Accra polo grounds. Its independence stressed pan-African unity and laid groundwork for liberation movements elsewhere on the continent.",
